<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Four Oirat</h1><p class="st-meta">1399 CE – 1634 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The confederation of western Mongol peoples that rivalled the Chinggisid khans for two centuries and captured a Ming emperor at Tumu in 1449.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a> were forest and steppe peoples of north-western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a> who had joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> early. After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> in 1368 they formed a union of four main groups, usually listed as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choros-oirats">Choros</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torghut">Torghut</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorbet">Dörbet</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khoshut-khanate">Khoshut</a>, and challenged the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-yuan">Northern Yuan</a> khans for leadership of the steppe.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The confederation was governed by an assembly of chiefs, and its leaders, not being descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, usually ruled through puppet khans. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toghon-taishi">Toghon</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esen-taishi">Esen</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> power in the 15th century; Esen defeated and captured the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming</a> emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengtong-emperor">Zhengtong</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumu-crisis">Tumu</a> in 1449 and briefly took the title of khan himself before being killed in 1455.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Pushed west by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayan-khan">Dayan Khan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altan-khan">Altan Khan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirats</a> moved towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dzungar-khanate">Dzungaria</a> in the 16th century and adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelug">Gelug Buddhism</a>. In the 1630s the confederation divided into the Dzungar Khanate, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kalmyk-khanate">Kalmyk Khanate</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khoshut-khanate">Khoshut Khanate</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tibet-1912-1951">Tibet</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 1399 CE – 1634 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.54%;width:4.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1399 CE – 1634 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Toghon, Esen Taishi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism, Tibetan Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oirat Mongolian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, <a href="/countries/china">China</a>, <a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oirat confederation, Dörben Oirat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1516&amp;focus=four-oirat" aria-label="Four Oirat on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7142 558 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Four Oirat lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y